Subject: dlm_init: the platform's registrations leave the core

dlm_init() registered ashnazag's guest major 59 (cpmguest) and called its
ds_modinit; the Amix kernels have neither.  What a platform registers at
boot belongs in its plat_dmainit(), which dmainit() already calls after
dlm_init() (weak and empty in dlm_cache.s until patch 0013; since then
only core/plat defines it).  Upstream would carry the two
calls in its own platform file (kernel/amiga/amigadlm.c there); ours are
core/plat/k30 and core/plat/k46.  30-module-core.md section 2, patch 1.

--- a/dlm_core.c
+++ b/dlm_core.c
@@ -1128,16 +1128,5 @@
 	dlm_ktab = dlm_ksym;
 	strcpy(dlm_path, dlm_defpath);
 	dlm_inited = 1;
-#ifndef DLM_HOST
-	if (dlm_creg("cpmguest", 59) != 0)
-		printf("dlm: cpmguest registration failed\n");
-	{
-		extern void ds_modinit();
-		void (*volatile init)() = ds_modinit;
-		__asm__(".weak ds_modinit");
-		if (init)
-			(*init)();
-	}
-#endif
 	printf("dlm: %d kernel symbols\n", (int)G32(dlm_ksym + KH_NSYM) - 1);
 }
